entifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","title":"Interaction_DragView","abstract":[{"text":"Reproduces the runner reference’s fixed layer hierarchy and framing. The card maps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" Position to its offset. Release projects momentum, applies the Drag","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch’s rubber-band bounds, and pulses Reset when both position axes are within the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"placed graph’s 100-point center tolerance.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"title":"Swami","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"}}}